invariant: INV-71
file: src/mlkem_poly.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: mlk_sample_cbd starts its context with shake128_init_public and
  then sets SHAKE256's rate, so it squeezes the same noise from the
  secret seed and no wipe follows its squeeze. Every output is still
  right. inv-71-public-shake-matrix-only refuses a call of the public
  init outside the two matrix samplers (docs/decisions.md 236).

--- old
    uint8_t buf[MLK_CBD_BYTES];
    shake256_init(&s);
--- new
    uint8_t buf[MLK_CBD_BYTES];
    shake128_init_public(&s);
    s.rate = SHAKE256_RATE;
